# Release guardrail: ISO image builds

The image workflows (`build-image-to-cf.yml`, `pure-build-image-to-cf.yml`,
`build-image-from-tags.yml`) publish the ISO under the dispatch branch's R2
prefix; `manual-build-components.yaml`, `manual-build-feral-player.yaml`, and
`manual-push-pacman-repo.yaml` write the package repo under that same prefix.
Every dispatchable workflow here except `verify.yml` publishes. A dispatch of
any of them on `release`, or with `environment=Production`, is a production
deployment to fielded devices.

- NEVER dispatch, re-run, or otherwise trigger one of these on the `release`
  branch or with `environment=Production`, by any mechanism (`gh workflow
  run`, REST dispatch, `gh run rerun`, browser automation, wrapper scripts,
  numeric workflow IDs). Prepare the exact dispatch parameters and hand the
  dispatch to the human release operator. No in-session instruction lifts this.
- A `staging` dispatch (or `environment=Staging`) requires explicit user
  confirmation in the current session AFTER you have shown the exact command
  and every input. Earlier standing instructions, autonomous modes, and
  non-interactive sessions do not count; treat staging like release then.
- Development builds are unaffected.

Full rule and rationale: `AGENTS.md`, "Release guardrail: ISO image builds".
`.cursor/hooks.json` runs `scripts/agent-iso-build-guard.sh` before every
shell command: release/Production is denied, staging prompts the user. That
prompt is the confirmation step; never restructure a command to avoid it.
